Directed by The DUFF 's Ari Sandel, the film follows a perennial bachelor whose carefree life is upended when he unexpectedly inherits his cousin's infant child. Just as he gets a grip on life as a dad, complications arise when the child's godmother appears around the holidays to claim custody of her. What ensues is a love story neither saw coming. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Tamara Chestna ( Something from Tiffany's , Moxie ) penned the script. Steve Barnett is producing for Monarch Media, alongside Mark Ross for Lincoln Road Films, Spencer Berman and Jonas for Powered by Jonas and Chestna. Alan Powell and Vicky Patel are exec producing for Monarch. Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Dodd took on the role of Francesca Bridgerton in Netflix's hit series from Shonda Rhimes in Season 3, reprising in the fourth installment before being set to co-lead Season 5 with Masali Baduza. The new season is due next year. Dodd comes to Netflix's new rom-com with feature credits including Enola Holmes 2 &#x2014; also from Netflix &#x2014; Marvel's Eternals and Fighting with My Family .

Last month, Dodd signed on to lead Miss You Forever, Zara Drake , a romantic drama marking the feature directorial debut of Lucas Jones. She is represented by Olivia Bell Management, Range Media Partners and Gang, Tyre, Ramer.

Cinematographers Barry Ackroyd and Christopher Ross are set to be honored by the British Society of Cinematographers . The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences will receive the BSC Bert Easey Technical Achievement Award.

Ackroyd, whose credits include &#x201C;The Hurt Locker&#x201D; and &#x201C;United 93,&#x201D; as well as collaborations with director Ken Loach, including &#x201C;Sweet Sixteen&#x201D; and &#x201C;The Wind That Shakes the Barley will receive the BSC's highest honor, the Lifetime Achievement Award, in recognition of a career spanning more than 40 years across film and television. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Ross will receive the Society's BSC John Alcott Award, sponsored by ARRI. This award recognizes an individual for their services to the Society.

Ross, who served as President of the British Society of Cinematographers between 2022 and 2026, helped revamp the BSC Education Series, the rejuvenation of the Q&A series, the restructuring of the Society's committees and overseeing growth in both membership and diversity.

The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences will receive the BSC Bert Easey Technical Achievement Award. Celebrating its 100th anniversary as an organization in 2027, the Academy has been a leading force in recognizing technical achievement and innovation, enabling and supporting filmmakers and contributing to the development of technical standards across our industry.

Among the Academy's many achievements are its contribution to the standardization of the 4:3 aspect ratio in the 1920s and 1930s, now commonly known as the &#x201C;Academy Ratio&#x201D;; the introduction of the Scientific and Technical Awards, which recognize the technicians and companies whose innovations make the films we see today possible; and the development of the Academy Color Encoding System (ACES), which provides a global, open-source standard for color management. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The Academy has also featured many technology-related exhibitions and programs at the Academy Museum of Motion Pictures and launched the Academy Marquee Theater List, which aims to celebrate cinemas that exemplify the moviegoing experience around the world, through audio-visual fidelity, diverse programming, community engagement and more.

In a statement, Oliver Stapleton BSC, President of the British Society of Cinematographers, commented: &#x201C;It is a great pleasure for us to recognize four very deserving recipients at this year's BSC Awards. Each, in their own way, has made an outstanding contribution to our industry and to the wider world of cinematography.&#x201D; He continued, &#x201C;Barry Ackroyd's extraordinary body of work has helped shape modern filmmaking and his contribution to cinematography over many decades is truly remarkable. Christopher Ross has given so much to the BSC, not only through his outstanding work as a cinematographer but also through his commitment, leadership and dedication during his time as President.&#x201D;

Stapleton said, &#x201C;The Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences has played an invaluable role in championing the art and science of filmmaking, celebrating technical innovation and supporting the creative community.&#x201D;

Pat McEnallay is set to receive the BSC Special Achievement Award. McEnallay has been a champion of young filmmakers and a trailblazer in the development of sustainable solutions for filmmaking.

McEnallay began his career working with companies such as Lee Lighting, Agfa and Panalux, supporting the development of new technologies and helping young cinematographers access the equipment they needed to make short films. Among those he supported were Lol Crawley, Ross and Ed Wild. He also serves as Co-Chair of the BSC Sustainability Committee and continues to support and enable the next generation of filmmakers.

Stapleton said, &#x201C;Pat McEnallay's generosity, enthusiasm and determination to support the next generation of filmmakers, alongside his pioneering work in sustainability, make him a hugely deserving recipient. What unites all four is their generosity of spirit and their commitment to making our industry better. On behalf of the BSC, I would like to congratulate them all and thank them for everything they have contributed to our craft and our community.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

The awards will be presented alongside the competitive awards at the 71st British Society of Cinematographers Awards on Feb. 6, 2027. The ceremony will be hosted by Edith Bowman and will take place in the Great Room at the Grosvenor House Hotel.

Jennifer Lopez has entered her &#x201C;happy era.&#x201D;

The singer-dancer-actress makes that perfectly clear in her new concert film, &#x201C;The JLo Show: Live in Las Vegas,&#x201D; with self-deprecating jokes about her much tabloidized love life.

&#x201C;If you take life too seriously, you'll be a miserable person,&#x201D; Lopez tells me during a recent conversation over Zoom. &#x201C;You have to find the humor in things, and you have to be honest with who you are &#x2014; not just all the great things about who you are, but all of the things that you you've done and the choices you've made that were questionable. We&#x2019;ve all made those.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'The Comeback King' Trailer: Glen Powell Is a Washed-Up Country Star in Judd Apatow's New Comedy Jessica Chastain Returning to Broadway in New Play 'Lost Lear'

Today, Lopez says, her life at 57 is &#x201C;unencumbered with any toxicity, it&#x2019;s unencumbered with any other kind of relationship in my life that is not healthy for me and so it&#x2019;s only the relationship with myself that I&#x2019;m dealing with right now.&#x201D;

&#x201C;I have gotten closer to God spiritually,&#x201D; she continues. &#x201C;I have gotten more self-aware, more appreciative of the little girl who grew up in the Bronx in front of that television &#x2026; It&#x2019;s been a very happy time and I think it may surprise people because they think, oh God, all this stuff happened again and it&#x2019;s like, no, no. It was the best thing that ever happened to me, and I&#x2019;m really grateful for where I am right now.&#x201D;

The concert chronicles Lopez&#x2019;s life story through a reimagining of some of her greatest hits and covers of others, including Lana Del Rey&#x2019;s &#x201C;Young and Beautiful&#x201D; and Elvis Presley&#x2019;s &#x201C;Heartbreak Hotel.&#x201D; She doesn&#x2019;t shy away from her fame, acknowledging all the scrutiny around her private life. She opens the show by joking in the decade since she had a Vegas residency, she&#x2019;d been married twice. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s not true, it&#x2019;s not true,&#x201D; Lopez says. &#x201C;It was only once &#x2014; felt like twice.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;Everybody thinks they know your life, and they don't,&#x201D; Lopez tells me. &#x201C;They really, really don't. And they will never really know the full story unless I decide to write a book one day.&#x201D;

That one day isn&#x2019;t happening anytime soon. &#x201C;Maybe when I&#x2019;m 98 years old,&#x201D; Lopez says, laughing. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s not something I have an interest in, giving all the details of other people and how they fit into my life. It&#x2019;s never been my thing. And trust me, there have been times when I&#x2019;ve wanted to say a thing or two about things.&#x201D;

In one of her most candid moments during the concert, Lopez reveals she turned to the late self-help guru Louise Hay for advice when she and Marc Anthony separated in 2011. Lopez first read Hay&#x2019;s 1984 bestseller &#x201C;You Can Heal Your Life&#x201D; when she was in her early 20s. &#x201C;I became obsessed with her because I realized I had control over my thoughts, which I don't think a lot of us realize in life,&#x201D; Lopez says. &#x201C;She changed my life in a lot of ways. So, when I was going through that very hard time when the kids were only little babies, three years old and I was going through a difficult separation and divorce, I called her.&#x201D;

In short, Hays likened romance to Lopez&#x2019;s dancing. &#x201C;She said, &#x2018;When you&#x2019;re learning to dance and you get the steps wrong, what do you do?&#x2019;&#x201D; Lopez recalls. &#x201C;I said, &#x2018;I just keep going until I get the steps right.&#x2019; And she said, &#x2018;That&#x2019;s it, Jennifer. Always keep dancing.&#x2019;&#x201D;

Not that Lopez is looking to jump into another relationship at the moment. It&#x2019;s been two years since she and Ben Affleck ended their two-year marriage .

&#x201C;It&#x2019;s not something I&#x2019;m thinking about because I've I think I&#x2019;ve learned a lot over the past 20 years, but also the past couple of years have really been about becoming more self-aware and really understanding what love is,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;I had a real idea about love as a little girl and moving through this crazy life that I found myself in, I realized that what I thought love was really isn&#x2019;t love.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Love is a secure, safe feeling,&#x201D; Lopez continues. &#x201C;Marriages, people can promise you the world and commit and do all the ceremonious things and do all these big gestures, but love is a different thing than that. It's a very different thing than that. So, the weddings and the marriages, I realize they're not the thing and even the promises are not the thing. It's the actions, it's the showing up, it's the understanding. It&#x2019;s not the leaving. It's the being consistent.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Or more simply put, Lopez says, &#x201C;I don't need to date. I'm good right now. I'm happy. I'm not trying to fuck it up.&#x201D;

&#x201C;The JLo Show: Live in Las Vegas&#x201D; premieres Nov. 26 at 8 p.m. ET/PT on CBS and Paramount+, with an extended version available exclusively on Paramount+.

Christopher Nolan told The Independent in a new interview to mark the home video release of " The Odyssey " that his record-breaking epic has "a lot of deleted scenes" that will never see the light of day. The Oscar winner does not believe in releasing director's cuts of his movies, meaning the deleted scenes were deleted for a reason and won't be seen by the public.

"There&#x2019;s a lot of deleted scenes scrumpled up in the wastebasket that no one will ever see," Nolan said. "I don&#x2019;t really believe in director&#x2019;s cuts. I want to stand by the film that goes out." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Ella Langley Breaks a CMA Awards Record by Winning Six in One Night, Including Entertainer of the Year: The Complete List of Winners Jessica Chastain Returning to Broadway in New Play 'Lost Lear'

"As a writer-director, I try to do a lot of that weeding out," he continued, "There aren&#x2019;t many scenes that were shot. On a film like this, to spend a day shooting something on top of a mountain or in the rain or on a boat or whatever that isn&#x2019;t gonna be in the film, I would really rather not do that. And so I wanna stand behind the cuts of the films that are put out there.&#x201D;

Nolan stressed that it's his job as the film's director "to fight for the cut of the movie right until it goes into theaters. That&#x2019;s what I&#x2019;ve always done."

Cillian Murphy memorbaly told Collider during the release of Nolan's last movie, "Oppenheimer," that no director's cut of the best picture winner would ever be seen because "there&#x2019;s no deleted scenes in Chris Nolan movies."

"That&#x2019;s why there are no DVD extras on his movies because the script is the movie," Murphy added at the time. "He knows exactly what&#x2019;s going to end up &#x2013; he&#x2019;s not fiddling around with it trying to change the story. That is the movie.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Another reason Nolan doesn't often have many deleted scenes in his movies is because he prioritizes shooting on celluloid film, which is expensive. The director goes into his film shoots knowing exactly what he needs to capture, nothing more and nothing less.

&#x201C;I tend to try and weed things out on paper because it&#x2019;s crazy expensive to shoot things that aren&#x2019;t going to be in the film,&#x201D; Nolan previously told MTV.com . &#x201C;It also takes up a lot of time and energy. Pretty much with all my films, there are very few deleted scenes, which always disappoints the DVD crowd.&#x201D;

"The Odyssey" opened in theaters over the summer and became Nolan's highest-grossing movie ever with $1.8 billion, also the highest-grossing R-rated release in history. The film is now positioned as an Oscar frontrunner for best picture and best director, among other nominations.

Hassan Al Thawadi , the Qatari lawyer who chairs the Qatar Film Committee and oversaw the 2022 FIFA World Cup soccer tournament, believes the Arab nation can become a major hub for international film production based on its track record hosting the global sports event.

&#x201C;Whenever a promise seems lofty,&#x201D; he said, one must remember Qatar &#x201C;delivered the World Cup.&#x201D;

Al Thawadi knows what he is talking about. He was directly involved in the delivery of the massive FIFA event back in 2022 as Managing Director of the Supreme Committee for Delivery and Legacy (SC), the Qatari government entity that was responsible for overseeing and coordinating efforts at both national and international levels for the soccer tournament. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories As CMA Awards Prepare 60th Annual Telecast, Retiring CEO Sarah Trahern Prepares for Her Exit, and Looks Back on Decades of Prime-Time Highlights 'Hunger Games' Companion Album to Feature Jennifer Lawrence, Ella Langley, Tyler Childers, Mckenna Grace and 25 More

The executive spoke at length about the lessons the Qatari film industry can learn from the World Cup during the opening talk at this year&#x2019;s Doha Industry Days , moderated by Variety &#x2019;s Nick Vivarelli.

&#x201C;I'm proud to say that the team that delivered the World Cup is now delivering major events all over the world and is a true legacy of 2022,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;Now that's the same core value; that's the same principle, and that's the same roadmap in the film industry," he added.

"A principle that serves as our north star in film. It's the blend and fusion of the local, regional and global that allows us to be a credible and successful platform and launchpad for cinema and content creation from the Arab world and the Global South and to ultimately achieve those loftier goals of bringing cultures together in an era where significant efforts are exerted into keeping us apart," Al Thawadi continued. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Last year&#x2019;s inaugural edition of the Doha Industry Days, the industry component of the revamped Doha Film Festival , saw the announcement of Qatar's 50% film and TV cash rebate, followed by several partnerships with major international players such as Neon and Paramount Skydance (now Skydance Corporation).

The Neon deal involves six to 10 feature films and shorts over four years that Neon will co-finance and distribute. As for Skydance, the partnership is through Miramax, the U.S. film and TV studio owned by Qatar&#x2019;s beIN Media Group and Ellison&#x2019;s company. That deal will germinate one original scripted series and one film. The agreement has already led to the development of an Arabic adaptation of Miramax&#x2019;s 2001 romantic comedy &#x201C;Serendipity.&#x201D;

&#x201C;When we gathered here a year ago, we spoke about an ambition to build a globally connected film ecosystem,&#x201D; said Al-Thawadi, who added: &#x201C;One year on, and that ambition is translating into tangible partners."

According to the exec, the Qatar Screen Production Incentive (QSPI) is already being &#x201C;used on the ground&#x201D; by major partners, including one flagship U.S. streamer currently shooting in Qatar &#x2014; although Al-Thawadi couldn&#x2019;t disclose further details on what streamer or what project just yet. The streamer is believed to be Netflix.

Al-Thawadi underlined how his strategic goal is different from similar efforts by neighbouring countries in that it aims not to necessarily attract physical production to the country, but to create a &#x201C;gateway&#x201D; for projects in the broader region. Productions shooting in other Arab countries can still access the Qatari rebate, although it then becomes capped at a&#x2014;still healthy&#x2014;25%. &#x201C;The idea is to set up in Qatar and get access to the entire region. And that's the most important part.&#x201D;

&#x201C;What we want to do is create the right ecosystem, the right infrastructure, the right regulatory infrastructure, the right partnerships for people to know that when they come to Qatar, they get access to everybody,&#x201D; he noted. &#x201C;They get access to Egypt, they get access to Saudi, and vice versa.&#x201D;

&#x201C;If we continue competing against each other, we'll never reach our full potential,&#x201D; the exec pointed out. &#x201C;The regional rebate's main purpose is to set up base in Qatar, have a certain element of Qatar, and have a certain center of gravity based on Qatar. But if you want to access the rest of the region, by all means [you can do so].&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Al-Thawadi is thinking long-term. He's transcending a five, or even ten-year, plan to think 20, 30 years ahead. In that sense, the Qatari exec sees the value of building an industry beyond the immediate benefits of physical production.

&#x201C;[The value] is built upon the other aspects. The financing, the insurance, the bonding, the training, the educational side of things," he said. "And so we're trying to create different elements of the industry on our side that complement what's already available in the region, and that allows us to reach global audiences.&#x201D;

The Film Committee chief admitted that recent geopolitical conflicts have affected the rolling out of high-profile projects in the country, but underlines how conversations with U.S. players such as Skydance and Neon have not cooled off. He teased further announcements regarding the country&#x2019;s partnership with Neon, to come in the next few days, and reiterated that he looks forward to understanding how these collaborations can go beyond production to discuss other key areas such as distribution, technology, and talent development.

The Doha Industry Days run November 19-21.

UPDATE: Barack and Michelle Obama's media company Higher Ground has signed on to serve as co-producers on the upcoming Off Broadway revival of Neil Simon &#x2019;s farce Rumors . The production, with direction Zhailon Levingston ( Cats: The Jellicle Ball) , features stars from two casts of Bravo&#x2019;s Real Housewives franchise.

&#x201C;Zhailon Levingston&#x2019;s reimagining of this beloved Neil Simon classic will be a dream come true for fans of reality TV and great theatre alike,&#x201D; said Michelle Obama, co-founder of Higher Ground, in a statement. &#x201C;As someone who&#x2019;s seen her share of Housewives drama, I can&#x2019;t imagine a better cast to serve up its secrets, gossip, and spiraling chaos. Our team at Higher Ground is thrilled to help bring this sharp, visionary production to life.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

